2026-09-07T00:00:06Z (RFD66606-2235) 'An ACP agent that plans with taskweft and executes through the editor
 # tags: rfd:details-title, rfd:no-final-newline
 Text:RFD2235  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-07T00:00:07Z (RFD66606-2235) 'The agent holds no language model. A prompt is a slash command or a phrase matched against the domain's method names; taskweft plans it; every step is one ACP tool call through the client's files and terminals behind a permission prompt; a failed step replans from the verified prefix or says that no other decomposition reaches the goal. Claude Code drives the same agent through an MCP bridge that is an ACP client, so the session keeps its context. Every request and update is an event in one `weft_fdb` database per session, the hosted door being the fabric-store writer and OpenBao's sqlite-fdb engine the fallback. The Fly door is gated by OpenBao tokens, never GitHub, and runs no step itself: executor sides dial in under a bao-held policy with a local override. `DETAILS.md` carries the rest.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2235  1 LINE
 Text:Written

